f7=A.ad(1,"Officer Navarro is as close to the cop ideal as you\u2019re going to get in the Precinct #1: honest, a believer in the public trust, and something of an icon to her fellow officers. Cavalry earned her handle and her cred being the first on scene to a whole lot of Officer Down calls. \n\nYet, while she\u2019s been in the Patrol Division for over five years, she hasn\u2019t bought into the toxic perspective so many Lawmen develop after time in the field. She still believes in the work, and she\u2019s damned good at it. \n\nShe\u2019s also a realist and will cooperate with outside agencies, although she stays frustratingly within the straight and narrow. When it comes down to brass tacks, she\u2019ll probably have your back in a firefight and then arrest you for any needless property damage afterwards. \n\nBut as shiny as Cavalry seems, she does have a crack in her chrome: Her wife\u2019s gambling problem has put her family in serious debt. Seems her mainline can\u2019t stay off the virtual card tables and might have a debt to a Fixer named Rex Royale. Is Cavalry\u2019s cooperation worth compromising a rare good cop? I recommend no. \n\nCavalry is more of an \u201cIn An Emergency, Break Glass\u201d kind of asset. Use with care.",B.cE,B.az,0,B.jp,"Officer Suri Navarro",!1,n,"Cavalry",B.asS,"","danger_gal_dossier/Lawmen_Officer1_Paintover.png",2,A.a([new A.ko(4,B.dX)],k),A.a([],g),p,A.a([A.a([new A.c(k9,B.a7,k9,6),new A.c(k9,B.y,k9,6),new A.c(k9,B.a3,k9,5),new A.c(k9,B.a9,k9,4),new A.c(k9,B.P,k9,5),new A.c(k9,B.F,k9,6),new A.c(k9,B.C,k9,6),new A.c(k9,B.D,k9,6),new A.c(k9,B.af,k9,3)],j)],i),f7,k9)
