i6=A.a([new A.O(s.B(),B.w,8,l1,k9),new A.O(s.B(),B.w,6,l4,k9),new A.O(s.B(),B.u,6,l5,k9)],m)
i6=A.ad(1,"This bloke loves all that goes bang, so I\u2019m not at all shocked he\u2019s living with Paddles. They\u2019re the perfect storm of violence, both up close and at a distance. Barely toxic at all. Penitent\u2019s fairly new to the squad and Cazadora insisted on a full personal interview before she even let him put his application in.\n\nHe worked in the past as muscle-for-hire but seemed to be bad luck for his crews. Deals he made went south, meetings blew up (literally, on occasion), and people ended up dead. Immediately before joining Trauma Team, he worked a turf war between a pair of minor boostergangs in North Heywood (not important who, both sides are toast). He pitched up with hangers-on to tackle a lone pair of the opposition, only it turns out they weren\u2019t gangers, they were a couple of cosplaying Execs walking on the wild side.\n\nSquad NC4-2 got the call and came in guns blazing. Penitent legged it but his mates weren\u2019t so lucky. Impressed by the Trauma Team crew and needing new work, Penitent tracked down Paddles, fanboyed his way into a meeting with Cazadora, and let his puppy-enthusiasm carry the day. Helps that he\u2019s a lot better with the AV\u2019s mounted weapons than Paddles (). Why all this work? Psych profile suggests, deep down, he knows he\u2019s useless alone, and NC4-2\u2019s a dog with big teeth to cling to.",B.cD,B.az,0,B.n6,"Squad Gunner",!1,p,"Penitent",B.atE,"","danger_gal_dossier/TraumaTeam_MedEvacPilot2_Paintover_v2.png",43,A.a([new A.cE(4,B.aw)],k),A.a([],g),n,A.a([A.a([new A.c(k9,B.a7,k9,4),new A.c(k9,B.y,k9,7),new A.c(k9,B.a3,k9,6),new A.c(k9,B.a9,k9,5),new A.c(k9,B.P,k9,4),new A.c(k9,B.F,k9,4),new A.c(k9,B.C,k9,6),new A.c(k9,B.D,k9,7),new A.c(k9,B.af,k9,5)],j)],i),i6,k9)
