s($,"dnY","vS",()=>{var q,p,o=null,n="When using this ammunition, you ablate armor by 2 instead of 1 whenever you would ablate armor. ",m="When using this ammunition, you deal no damage with your attack. Anyone meat hit by your attack must instead attempt to beat a DV15 Resist Torture/Drugs Check. Anyone who fails is dealt 3d6 damage directly to their HP. Their armor isn't ablated because it wasn't interacted with.",l="When using this ammunition, whenever you cause the Foreign Object Critical Injury, the victim rolls again on the Critical Injury table (see pg. 187 of the rulebook) until they roll a Critical Injury that isn't Foreign Object. The victim then suffers that Critical Injury as well. This second injury deals no Bonus Damage.",k="When using this ammunition, whenever you deal damage to a target through their armor, you ignite the target. Until your target spends an Action to put themselves out, they take 2 damage directly to their HP whenever they end their Turn. Multiple instances of this effect cannot stack.",j="When using this ammunition, you deal no damage with your attack. Anyone meat hit by your attack must instead attempt to beat a DV13 Resist Torture/Drugs Check. Anyone who fails is dealt 2d6 damage directly to their HP. Their armor isn't ablated because it wasn't interacted with.",i="Damage dealt using this ammunition cannot cause a Critical Injury. Additionally, attacks made with this ammunition cannot ablate armor. If damage dealt by this ammunition would reduce a target with more than 1 HP to less than 0 HP, they are instead left at 1 HP. Rubber Ammunition counts as Basic Ammunition for the purposes of use with Exotic Weapons.",h="When using this ammunition, you deal no damage with your attack. Anyone meat hit by your attack must instead attempt to beat a DV13 Resist Torture/Drugs Check. Anyone who fails is now Prone (see pg. 169 of the rulebook) and Unconscious for 1 minute or until they are woken by taking damage, or by someone else using an Action that touches them.",g="Targeting Scope Cyberware is required in order to make use of Smart Ammunition. When fired by a User without Targeting Scope Cyberware, Smart Ammunition won't fire even when the trigger is pulled, as a safety feature. When using this ammunition, whenever you miss a shot by 4 or less when using a weapon's single shot firing mode, your missed shot immediately has a second chance to hit your target. This second chance to hit is made by rolling again to hit the exact same shot DV on the range table which you missed, except that you add 10 to the d10 instead of anything you would typically add to the Check, with the only exception being LUCK. A target that can dodge bullets can choose to dodge this ranged attack as normal.",f="\u201cThese can get a lot done on a budget. Also good for target practice, but I think I heard Molly mention that already. You did already win a bunch too, so I\u2019d be surprised if you wanted more. Yeah, we can probably move on.\u201d\n\nDamage dealt by a weapon loaded with Junk Ammunition is reduced by 1d6 (minimum 1d6) against any target with 1 or more SP when fired in Single Shot, and the Autofire Rating of any weapon firing Junk Ammunition is reduced by 1 to a minimum of Autofire (3). Any weapon capable of firing Basic Ammunition can load Junk Ammunition.",e="\u201cGood for hunting. There may not be many birds around anymore but there are still plenty of rodents ripe for the taking in Night City if you know where to look. Protein is protein.\u201d\n\nA weapon loaded with Small Game Ammunition deals 2d6 less damage (minimum 1d6) with each bullet fired in Single Shot and the Autofire Rating of any weapon firing Small Game Ammunition is reduced by 1 to a minimum of Autofire (3). Any weapon capable of firing Basic Ammunition can load Small Game Ammunition.",d="The best ammunition for Smart Weapons.\n\nImproved Smart Ammunition only operates in a weapon designated as a Smart Weapon \u2013 this does not include weapons with a Smartgun Link attachment. When using Improved Smart Ammunition, the user ignores all penalties due to darkness, smoke, fog, or any type of visual obscurement. \n\nAdditionally, whenever the user misses a ranged attack DV by 5 or less while using this weapon, they can immediately try to hit that target again.\n\nWhen the user makes this second attempt, they add 14 to your roll (remember, they can still add LUCK) instead of the standard STAT + Skill + any bonuses against the DV from  the original attack. All penalties from their first shot carry over to their second attempt.",c="Say you really don\u2019t like someone, and you want to make this very clear to them. Swap out your magazine for one with some of these. The medical bills alone will make them wish you had bought explosive ammunition from me instead.\n\nCritical Injuries caused by this ammunition cannot be Quick Fixed unless a Quick Fix would remove the Injury effect permanently. The DV to perform a Quick Fix or Treatment on a Critical Injury caused by this ammunition is increased by 2.",b="KaBOOM! This ammunition will send body parts flying clean off into the next district over when you sweep your street. It\u2019s a whole new way to celebrate the fourth of July every single day of the year. It even comes in arrows, too! Isn\u2019t that neat?\n\nThis ammunition can not be used to make an Aimed Shot. Attacks made with this ammunition are at a -2 penalty. When using this ammunition, 5\u2019s are treated as 6\u2019s on your damage dice solely for the purpose of determining if your attack causes a Critical Injury.",a="I carry these because people ask for them specifically. Confident mercenary types, like yourself, prefer them for stuff like low drag, tight shot groupings, apogee, coriolis effect, bullet harmonics, stuff like that. I don\u2019t understand all the finer details. I\u2019m just a guy who sells them.\n\nTo utilize this ammunition, a user must have either a Skill Level 7 or higher in the appropriate weapon or a Combat Awareness Rank 1 or higher. Users meeting one of these requirements who attack with a weapon loaded with this ammunition add +1 to their Attack Check when firing in Single Shot Mode or +2 to their Attack Check when making an Aimed Shot.",a0="These are trusted by real professionals, these ones right here. I forget their names, but you know the ones. You can hardly see these things come out the barrel, they\u2019re going so fast. Even the finest speedware isn\u2019t going to save you from these babies.\n\nAnyone attempting to dodge an attack made with this ammunition suffers a -2 penalty to their Skill Check.",a1="Now, I\u2019m not a scientist. Professionally, I\u2019m more of a business lunatic, but I swear these things work like magic. It\u2019s just gotta be, because even though they\u2019re small, they leave big holes in people every time, voila, like magic. You can even get them in shotgun shells!\n\nWhenever this ammunition causes a Critical Injury, the victim rolls a second time on the Critical Injury table until they roll a Critical Injury they aren\u2019t currently suffering. They then suffer this Critical Injury as well. This second Injury deals no Bonus Damage.",a2="Sensible and reliable. The way I see it, for breakfast, you could eat a plain bagel, but who wants that? These here are the sesame seed bagels of ammunition. They leave your enemies just as toasted to perfection, but with a little extra flavor.\n\nThe first time this ammunition causes a Critical Injury during an Attack, the target\u2019s Base Death Save Penalty increases by 1. This is in addition to any increase caused by the Critical Injury itself. In addition, if the Critical Injury is Foreign Object, the victim rolls again on the Critical Injury table until they roll a Critical Injury that isn\u2019t Foreign Object. The Victim then suffers that Critical Injury as well. This second Injury deals Bonus Damage.",a3="These bullets glow like a second sun, even at high noon. Staying on target is as easy as walking the light show directly into your least favorite person.\n\nWhen firing a weapon loaded with this ammunition in Autofire Mode, a user adds +1 to their Skill Check.",a4=A.a([A.bf(B.xP,"Acid Paintball","Acid Paintball deals no damage, but lowers the SP of the target's armor (worn in the location shot) by one with each successful hit. Great for trying to capture someone alive.",10,B.qc,B.Oy,0,o,0,B.x,o,!1),A.bf(B.O9,"Armor-Piercing Medium Pistol",n,100,B.dq,B.p3,0,o,0,B.x,o,!1),A.bf(B.jf,"Armor-Piercing Heavy Pistol",n,100,B.d6,B.p3,0,o,0,B.x,o,!1),A.bf(B.qe,"Armor-Piercing Very Heavy Pistol",n,100,B.dJ,B.p3,0,o,0,B.x,o,!1),A.bf(B.lL,"Armor-Piercing Rifle",n,100,B.cg,B.p3,0,o,0,B.x,o,!1),A.bf(B.nW,"Armor-Piercing Slug",n,100,B.fB,B.p3,0,o,0,B.x,o,!1),A.bf(B.CT,"Armor-Piercing Arrow",n,100,B.dQ,B.p3,0,o,0,B.x,o,!1),A.bf(B.im,"Armor-Piercing Grenade",n,100,B.de,B.p3,0,6,0,B.x,o,!1),A.bf(B.qd,"Armor-Piercing Rocket",n,100,B.h4,B.p3,0,o,0,B.x,o,!1),A.bf(B.jM,"Basic Medium Pistol","This is the standard ammunition for Medium Pistols & SMGs. It has no special features.",10,B.dq,B.eT,0,o,0,B.x,o,!1),A.bf(B.ct,"Basic Heavy Pistol","This is the standard ammunition for Heavy Pistols & Heavy SMGs. It has no special features.",10,B.d6,B.eT,0,o,0,B.x,o,!1),A.bf(B.bm,"Basic Very Heavy Pistol","This is the standard ammunition for Very Heavy Pistols. It has no special features.",10,B.dJ,B.eT,0,o,0,B.x,o,!1),A.bf(B.dR,"Basic Rifle","This is the standard ammunition for Rifles and Sniper Rifles. It has no special features.",10,B.cg,B.eT,0,o,0,B.x,o,!1),A.bf(B.i2,"Basic Slug","This is the standard ammunition for Shotguns. It has no special features.",10,B.fB,B.eT,0,o,0,B.x,o,!1),A.bf(B.l0,"Basic Shotgun Shell","In addition to Slugs, Shotguns can also fire Shotgun Shells. You can't make an Aimed Shot with a Shotgun Shell. When you fire a Shotgun Shell, you make 1 Ranged Attack (REF + Shoulder Arms + 1d10) vs. a DV13. If successful every target in front of you, within 6m/yds (3 squares), that you can see, takes 3d6 damage if you hit. You roll damage once for all targets. Individual targets with REF 8 or Higher can still choose to attempt to dodge your Shotgun Shell.",10,B.ea,B.eT,0,3,0,B.x,o,!0),A.bf(B.uG,"Basic Arrow","This is the standard ammunition for Bows & Crossbows. It has no special features.",10,B.dQ,B.eT,0,o,0,B.x,o,!1),A.bf(B.NS,"Basic Paintball","This is the standard ammunition for Air Pistols. It has no special features.",10,B.qc,B.eT,0,o,0,B.x,o,!1),A.bf(B.NR,"Battery Pack","An easily rechargeable battery pack. Powers energy weapons such as the Stun Baton and Stun Gun.",50,B.nU,B.eT,0,o,0,B.x,o,!1),A.bf(B.NF,"Biotoxin Arrow",m,500,B.dQ,B.a41,0,3,0,B.x,o,!1),A.bf(B.D_,"Biotoxin Grenade",m,500,B.de,B.a41,0,3,0,B.x,o,!0),A.bf(B.uC,"EMP Grenade","When using this ammunition, you deal no damage with your attack. Anyone hit by your attack must instead attempt to beat a DV15 Cybertech Check. If they fail, the GM chooses 2 pieces of their Cyberware or carried electronics to become inoperable for 1 minute. Cyberlimbs that are rendered inoperable act as their meat counterparts do when they have been dismembered, but they still hang loosely.",500,B.de,B.aIe,0,0,0,B.x,o,!0),A.bf(B.NG,"Expansive Medium Pistol",l,100,B.dq,B.rQ,0,o,0,B.x,o,!1),A.bf(B.xM,"Expansive Heavy Pistol",l,100,B.d6,B.rQ,0,o,0,B.x,o,!1),A.bf(B.xN,"Expansive Very Heavy Pistol",l,100,B.dJ,B.rQ,0,o,0,B.x,o,!1),A.bf(B.D1,"Expansive Rifle",l,100,B.cg,B.rQ,0,o,0,B.x,o,!1),A.bf(B.D0,"Expansive Slug",l,100,B.fB,B.rQ,0,o,0,B.x,o,!1),A.bf(B.NH,"Expansive Arrow",l,100,B.dQ,B.rQ,0,o,0,B.x,o,!1),A.bf(B.i1,"Flashbang Grenade","When using this ammunition, you deal no damage with your attack. Anyone hit by your attack must instead attempt to beat a DV15 Resist Torture/Drugs Check. Anyone who fails suffers the Damaged Eye and Damaged Ear Critical Injuries (see pg. 188) for the next minute. You do not take the Bonus Damage from the Critical Injuries.",100,B.de,B.aIf,0,0,0,B.x,o,!0),A.bf(B.D2,"Incendiary Medium Pistol",k,100,B.dq,B.qf,0,o,0,B.x,o,!1),A.bf(B.uD,"Incendiary Heavy Pistol",k,100,B.d6,B.qf,0,o,0,B.x,o,!1),A.bf(B.uE,"Incendiary Very Heavy Pistol",k,100,B.dJ,B.qf,0,o,0,B.x,o,!1),A.bf(B.D3,"Incendiary Rifle",k,100,B.cg,B.qf,0,o,0,B.x,o,!1),A.bf(B.p0,"Incendiary Shotgun Shell",k,100,B.ea,B.qf,0,3,0,B.x,o,!0),A.bf(B.NI,"Incendiary Arrow",k,100,B.dQ,B.qf,0,o,0,B.x,o,!1),A.bf(B.p1,"Incendiary Grenade",k,100,B.de,B.qf,0,6,0,B.x,o,!1),A.bf(B.NJ,"Poison Arrow",j,100,B.dQ,B.a42,0,2,0,B.x,o,!0),A.bf(B.D4,"Poison Grenade",j,100,B.de,B.a42,0,2,0,B.x,o,!0),A.bf(B.NK,"Rubber Medium Pistol",i,10,B.dq,B.uL,0,o,0,B.x,o,!1),A.bf(B.D5,"Rubber Heavy Pistol",i,10,B.d6,B.uL,0,o,0,B.x,o,!1),A.bf(B.uF,"Rubber Very Heavy Pistol",i,10,B.dJ,B.uL,0,o,0,B.x,o,!1),A.bf(B.D6,"Rubber Rifle",i,10,B.cg,B.uL,0,o,0,B.x,o,!1),A.bf(B.NL,"Rubber Slug",i,10,B.fB,B.uL,0,o,0,B.x,o,!1),A.bf(B.NM,"Rubber Arrow",i,10,B.dQ,B.uL,0,o,0,B.x,o,!1),A.bf(B.D7,"Sleep Arrow",h,500,B.dQ,B.a43,0,-1,0,B.x,o,!1),A.bf(B.xO,"Sleep Grenade",h,500,B.de,B.a43,0,0,0,B.x,o,!0),A.bf(B.NN,"Smart Medium Pistol",g,500,B.dq,B.uM,0,o,0,B.x,o,!1),A.bf(B.D8,"Smart Heavy Pistol",g,500,B.d6,B.uM,0,o,0,B.x,o,!1),A.bf(B.NO,"Smart Very Heavy Pistol",g,500,B.dJ,B.uM,0,o,0,B.x,o,!1),A.bf(B.D9,"Smart Rifle",g,500,B.cg,B.uM,0,o,0,B.x,o,!1),A.bf(B.NP,"Smart Arrow",g,500,B.dQ,B.uM,0,o,0,B.x,o,!1),A.bf(B.NQ,"Smart Rocket",g,500,B.h4,B.uM,0,o,0,B.x,o,!1),A.bf(B.io,"Smoke Grenade","When using this ammunition, you deal no damage with your attack. Obscures a 10m/yd by 10m/yd area with smoke for a minute on impact. The typical penalty for trying to perform a task obscured by smoke is -4.",50,B.de,B.a44,0,0,0,B.x,o,!0),A.bf(B.p2,"Teargas Grenade","When using this ammunition, you deal no damage with your attack. Anyone with meat eyes hit by your attack must instead attempt to beat a DV13 Resist Torture/Drugs Check. Anyone who fails suffers the Damaged Eye Critical injury (see pg. 188 of the rulebook) for the next minute. You do not take the Bonus Damage from the Critical Injury",50,B.de,B.aIi,0,0,0,B.x,o,!0),A.bf(B.NT,"KTech Doberman 500 Marking Scent","It didn\u2019t take long for security forces at SovOil to realize the benefits of the KTech Doberman 500\u2019s Tracking Mode. It also didn\u2019t take long for the dissidents they were tracking to engineer clever ways to throw the drone off their scent. Boosting the Doberman 500\u2019s olfactory sensors wasn\u2019t an option, so KTech developed a work around: a scent marker, undetectable to the baseline human nose, for the drone to lock onto. Referred to as \u201cdoberman piss\u201d by some, this marking scent made it easy for SovOil security to mark protesters at rallies and then track them to their lairs at their leisure.\n\nDoberman 500 Marking Scent is a unique form of ammunition for the Air Pistol (see CP:R page 347). It does no damage but, instead, marks the target with a scent they can\u2019t wash off except by dousing themselves in alcohol. The scent lasts 24 hours before wearing off naturally. Doberman 500 drones tracking a target marked with the scent gain a +4 to their Tracking Skill Check. Others with enhanced capabilities, such as biological bloodhounds and humans with Olfactory Boost chipware gain a +2 to their Tracking Skill Check when tracking a target marked with the scent. Comes in packs of 12.",50,B.qc,B.eT,0,0,0,B.ak,u.oK,!0),A.bf(B.NU,"Arachnid Grenade","The Arachnid is a non-lethal net grenade designed by the big brains at Centurion Essentials. This spherical explosive is filled with a highly flexible and sticky solution. Thirty seconds after exposure to oxygen, the solution takes on a rubbery consistency that remains sticky, making it almost impossible for anyone to move while covered in the material. So, when the Arachnid goes off, it makes a major mess.\n\nThe Arachnid\u2019s round design and purple chrome casing make it instantly recognizable in combat situations. The Arachnid is great for parties, prisons, and riots, with webbing in many fun colors. The CE Arachnid may be purchased at any Centurion Essentials kiosk or licensed retailer.\n\nThis is Grenade Ammunition. It can be loaded into a Grenade Launcher or thrown. Anyone hit by the grenade takes no damage but is covered by the Arachnid solution. Targets covered that do not take an Action to douse themselves in alcohol within the 30-second arming period (10 rounds in combat) or who are not covered in alcohol by someone else taking an Action to do so are grappled by it when it comes online.\n\nWhile grappled by the solution, targets cannot use their Move Action. Targets also can\u2019t make use of a weapon that requires two hands and take \u22122 to all Actions for as long as they remain grappled. The webbing solution surrounding a single target has 15 HP and is destroyed beyond repair when it reaches 0 HP. Firing a ranged weapon into an activated solution from outside of it deals damage to both the webbing and the person grappled by it. Destroying and escaping the webbing requires a DV15 Brawling Check that can be attempted by anyone within melee range.",100,B.de,B.eT,0,0,0,B.ak,"black_chrome/CenturionEssentials_ArachnidGrenade_JeffMcDonald_weapon_CRBC102_forWEB.jpg",!0),A.bf(B.NV,"GunMart Door Cracker","The GunMart Door Cracker is a cheap explosive device made for hard entry. The bomb itself is 1 inch (2.54 cm) in diameter and 1 inch (2.54 cm) thick. The base is magnetic with sticky tape around its edges in case the door (or wall or whatever) isn\u2019t metal. GunMart Door Crackers are popular with police and gangs alike and priced cheaply enough to be affordable to both.\n\nThis is an Explosive. It takes 30 seconds (10 Rounds in combat) to set up on a 2 m/yd by 2 m/yd section of cover and arm. This can be reduced to 1 Action with a DV15 Demolitions Check, which can only be attempted once.\n\nOnce armed, it can be detonated with an Action, via a dedicated detonation switch or a paired Agent. Upon detonation, the 2 m/yd by 2 m/yd section of cover, and only that section of cover, takes 6d6 damage.",50,B.de,B.eT,0,6,0,B.ak,"black_chrome/GunMart_DoorCracker_3BitStudios_weapon_CRBC104_forWEB.jpg",!1),A.bf(B.NW,"KillChip 100 Micro-Bomb","The origin of the KillChip 100 has been a mystery since the first one exploded a head during the 4th Corporate War. The KillChip looks just like a standard memory chip, and reads like it too when plugged into an Agent. When plugged into Chipware Socket Neuralware, however, it detonates. Law enforcement and intelligence agencies have been looking for the original source of the KillChip for the years with no luck. By now, thousands of KillChips have flooded the streets, making the technology easy to reverse-engineer.\n\nThis is an Explosive. A KillChip is an explosive standard memory chip that only detonates when plugged into Chipware Socket Neuralware. The unlucky person who inserts one into their head immediately takes 6d6 damage directly to their HP (armor does not reduce it) and suffers the Brain Injury Critical Injury. A DV15 Criminology, Cybertech, Demolitions, Electronics/Security Tech, or DV21 Perception Check reveals the KillChip as a dangerous explosive.",100,B.de,B.eT,0,6,0,B.ak,"black_chrome/KillChip100MicroBomb_3BitStudios_weapon_CRBC106_forWEB.jpg",!1),A.bf(B.NX,"KTech Security Grenade","KTech Security Grenades are carried primarily by SovOil naval security units aboard ships where fire and explosions can be a significant concern. These pineapple-style grenades offer a large bang but carry no risk of rupturing fuel tanks and damaging the extremely flammable petroleum within.\n\nIn other words, one SovOil security trooper standing on the deck outside the bridge can pop these babies out of a grenade launcher at mobs of pirates below all day and not worry about hurting the company\u2019s profit margins.\n\nThis is Grenade Ammunition. It can be loaded into a Grenade Launcher or thrown. It is an Armor Piercing Grenade that deals 5d6 damage to targets but causes no damage to cover.",100,B.de,B.eT,0,5,0,B.ak,"black_chrome/SecurityGrenade_AlvarVidal_weapon_CRBC107_KTech_forWEB.jpg",!1),A.bf(B.NY,"Micro Hydrogen Combuster","The Hydrosubsidium Micro Hydrogen Combustor is a small explosive device designed for deployment in full bottles. All units are rigged with a thirty-second timer that begins the countdown once the device is submerged entirely in liquid. The device then superheats, causing the bottle and its contents to explode violently. The resulting explosion sprays ultra-hot fluids and steam over everything in the blast radius. The Micro Hydrogen Combustor is popular with burgling Netrunners and covert operators. Just one can create a hell of a distraction.\n\nThis is an Explosive. The Hydrosubsidium Micro Hydrogen Combustor explodes like an Armor Piercing Grenade 30 seconds (10 Rounds in combat) after it is submerged entirely in liquid. Upon detonation, it also obscures the area of the 10m/yds by 10m/yds explosion with a thick cloud of steam for 1 minute. The typical penalty for trying to perform a task obscured in such a way is \u22124.",500,B.de,B.eT,0,6,0,B.ak,"black_chrome/Hydrosubsidium_MicroHydrogenCombustor_3BitStudios_weapon_CRBC105_forWEB.jpg",!1),A.bf(B.NZ,"OUTLet Explosive","An OUTLet Explosive looks just like a standard outlet adapter, but it\u2019s actually a small yet powerful micro-explosive. When plugged into a wall socket the OUTLet can be set to detonate via a remote trigger. The explosive burns hot and, in most cases, makes it look like victims died due to an electrical fire. \n\nIt was only after a hit in Night City that a fire investigator realized the true nature of the OUTLet. When word got out, dozens of murder investigations were re-opened worldwide.\n\nThis is an Explosive disguised as an outlet adapter. It takes 30 seconds (10 rounds in combat) to arm. This can be reduced to 1 Action with a DV15 Demolitions Check, which can only be attempted once. Once armed, it can be detonated as if it were an Armor Piercing Grenade with an Action, via a dedicated remote detonation switch or a paired Agent. A DV15 Criminology, Demolitions, or Electronics/Security Tech or a DV21 Perception Check reveals the OUTLet as a dangerous explosive.",100,B.de,B.eT,0,6,0,B.ak,"black_chrome/OUTLetexplosive_GuglielmoMeacci_weapon_CRBC108_forWEB.jpg",!1),A.bf(B.O_,"Shuriken Tornado Grenade","When Great Lakes Cutlery decided to get into the arms business, they did it with the Shuriken Tornado. This pineapple-style grenade is packed tightly with stacked shuriken and high-powered electromagnets. The base is weighted, so it always lands in a perfect standing position. Once activated and thrown, as the grenade lands and rests, the electromagnet activates, sending twenty shuriken exploding outward at high velocity. The force is so great the shuriken penetrate concrete and shred flesh and bone. The grenade gets the \u201ctornado\u201d in its name from the aftermath of the detonation since it looks like one hit the area.\n\nThis is Grenade Ammunition and does damage like an Armor Piercing Grenade. It can be loaded into a Grenade Launcher or thrown. Unlike with other explosions, the damage dealt by the Shuriken Tornado is rolled separately for each target damaged by it. Whenever damage caused by this grenade causes the Foreign Object Critical Injury, the victim rolls again on the Critical Injury table until they roll a Critical Injury that isn\u2019t Foreign Object. The victim then suffers that Critical Injury as well. This second injury deals no Bonus Damage",100,B.de,B.eT,0,6,0,B.ak,"black_chrome/GreatLakesCutlery_ShurikenTornadoGranade_3BitStudios_weapon_CRBC103_forWEB.jpg",!1),A.bf(B.O0,"TR-4 Detonator Fluid","TR-4 Detonator Fluid is a reactionary liquid capable of transforming ordinary CHOOH2 into a super explosive devastating to vehicles. To use TR-4, all one must do is pour the fluid into a fuel tank, where it mixes with the CHOOH2. When the vehicle starts, the mix flows to the engine where it fires and detonates. TR-4 is completely undetectable without full chemical analysis and has no smell. The detonator fluid was originally manufactured by Yakuza-funded scientists to create a new method of assassinating enemies. The fluid has since been reverse-engineered and almost any chemical Tech can create a batch.\n\nThis is an Explosive. TR-4 Detonator Fluid is a vial of pale yellow liquid which must be first poured into a vehicle\u2019s CHOOH2 tank to arm it. Doing this takes 30 seconds (10 rounds in combat). This can be reduced to 1 Action with a DV15 Demolitions Check, which can only be attempted once. Typically, you can\u2019t access the vehicle\u2019s tank without being able to start the vehicle yourself. Once mixed in, the next time the vehicle is started, the gas tank explodes like an Armor Piercing grenade. This explosion ignores any armor the vehicle has and automatically target\u2019s the vehicle\u2019s weak point for double damage.",500,B.de,B.eT,0,6,0,B.ak,"black_chrome/T-R4DetonatorFluid_3BitStudios_weapon_CRBC109_forWEB.jpg",!1),A.bf(B.O1,"Arasaka Acid","When coated with Arasaka Acid, the Weeping Reaver ablates armor by 2 instead of 1 whenever it would ablate armor.",100,B.xK,B.Oy,0,o,0,B.ak,o,!1),A.bf(B.O2,"Arasaka Fire","When coated with Arasaka Fire, whenever a user deals damage to a target through their armor, they ignite the target. Until the target spends an Action to put themselves out, they take 2 damage to their HP whenever they end their Turn. Multiple instances of this effect cannot stack.",100,B.xK,B.qf,0,o,0,B.ak,o,!1),A.bf(B.O3,"Arasaka Wound Salt","When coated with Arasaka Wound Salt, whenever the weapon causes the Foreign Object Critical Injury, the victim rolls again on the Critical Injury table until they roll a Critical Injury that isn\u2019t Foreign Object. The victim then suffers that Critical Injury as well. This second injury deals no Bonus Damage.",100,B.xK,B.rQ,0,o,0,B.ak,o,!1),A.bf(B.O6,"Sternmeyer Basic","Special ammo for the Sternmeyer M-02 Heavy Rifle.",500,B.CS,B.eT,0,o,0,B.iY,o,!1),A.bf(B.O7,"Nomad Air Cannon Acid","Special ammo for the Nomad Air Cannon. All armor worn by any coated target is reduced by 1 SP.",10,B.N_,B.Oy,0,o,0,B.iY,o,!1),A.bf(B.O4,"Rock","",0,B.CR,B.eT,0,o,0,B.ak,o,!1),A.bf(B.O5,"Harpoon","",10,B.xJ,B.eT,0,o,0,B.iY,o,!1),A.bf(B.O8,"Bullet to Slug Adapter Casings","Converts bullet Ammunition into Shotgun Slugs.",100,B.fB,B.eT,0,o,0,B.fa,o,!1),A.bf(B.Oa,"Junk Arrows",f,10,B.dQ,B.rR,0,o,-1,B.fa,o,!1),A.bf(B.uH,"Junk Heavy Pistol",f,10,B.d6,B.rR,-1,o,-1,B.fa,o,!1),A.bf(B.uI,"Junk Medium Pistol",f,10,B.dq,B.rR,-1,o,-1,B.fa,o,!1),A.bf(B.Da,"Junk Rifle",f,10,B.cg,B.rR,-1,o,-1,B.fa,o,!1),A.bf(B.Db,"Junk Shotgun Shell",f,10,B.ea,B.rR,0,2,0,B.fa,o,!0),A.bf(B.Ob,"Junk Slug",f,10,B.fB,B.rR,-1,o,-1,B.fa,o,!1),A.bf(B.Oc,"Junk Very Heavy Pistol",f,10,B.dJ,B.rR,-1,o,-1,B.fa,o,!1),A.bf(B.Od,"Small Game Heavy Pistol",e,10,B.d6,B.xR,-1,o,-2,B.fa,o,!1),A.bf(B.Oe,"Small Game Medium Pistol",e,10,B.dq,B.xR,-1,o,-2,B.fa,o,!1),A.bf(B.Of,"Small Game Rifle",e,10,B.cg,B.xR,-1,o,-2,B.fa,o,!1),A.bf(B.Og,"Small Game Shotgun Shell",e,10,B.ea,B.xR,0,1,0,B.fa,o,!0),A.bf(B.Oh,"Small Game Very Heavy Pistol",e,10,B.dJ,B.xR,-1,o,-2,B.fa,o,!1),A.bf(B.Oi,"Small Game",e,10,B.xL,B.eT,-1,o,-2,B.fa,o,!1),A.bf(B.Dc,"Molotov Cocktail","\u201cWhy are we selling these? This is so dangerous. Sigh.\u201d\n\nCan\u2019t be loaded into a Grenade Launcher. An Incendiary Grenade that deals 5d6 damage. While a Molotov cocktail is being carried by a character, if that unlucky choomba takes any damage that penetrates their armor, all Molotov Cocktails on their person have a 50% chance of being destroyed beyond repair. \n\nIf that happens, it doesn\u2019t explode but does set the choomba Deadly on Fire (see CP:R page 180) and destroys beyond repair all other Molotov Cocktails they\u2019re carrying.",20,B.de,B.aIg,0,5,0,B.fa,o,!1),A.bf(B.Oj,"Improved Smart Arrow",d,50,B.dQ,B.nX,0,o,0,B.ej,o,!1),A.bf(B.Ok,"Improved Smart Heavy Pistol",d,50,B.d6,B.nX,0,o,0,B.ej,o,!1),A.bf(B.Ol,"Improved Smart Medium Pistol",d,50,B.dq,B.nX,0,o,0,B.ej,o,!1),A.bf(B.Om,"Improved Smart Rifle",d,50,B.cg,B.nX,0,o,0,B.ej,o,!1),A.bf(B.xQ,"Improved Smart Shotgun Shell",d,50,B.ea,B.nX,0,3,0,B.ej,o,!0),A.bf(B.On,"Improved Smart Slug",d,50,B.fB,B.nX,0,o,0,B.ej,o,!1),A.bf(B.Oo,"Improved Smart Very Heavy Pistol",d,50,B.dJ,B.nX,0,o,0,B.ej,o,!1),A.bf(B.Op,"Improved Smart Grenade",d,500,B.de,B.nX,0,o,0,B.ej,o,!1),A.bf(B.Oq,"Improved Smart Rocket",d,500,B.h4,B.nX,0,o,0,B.ej,o,!1),A.bf(B.Or,"Burrowing Medium Pistol",c,40,B.dq,B.rP,0,o,0,B.aQ,o,!1),A.bf(B.Os,"Burrowing  Heavy Pistol",c,40,B.d6,B.rP,0,o,0,B.aQ,o,!1),A.bf(B.Ot,"Burrowing Very Heavy Pistol",c,40,B.dJ,B.rP,0,o,0,B.aQ,o,!1),A.bf(B.Ou,"Burrowing Slug",c,40,B.fB,B.rP,0,o,0,B.aQ,o,!1),A.bf(B.Ov,"Burrowing Rifle",c,40,B.cg,B.rP,0,o,0,B.aQ,o,!1),A.bf(B.Ow,"Burrowing Shotgun Shell",c,40,B.ea,B.rP,0,o,0,B.aQ,o,!1),A.bf(B.Ox,"Burrowing Arrow",c,40,B.dQ,B.rP,0,o,0,B.aQ,o,!1),A.bf(B.N0,"Explosive Medium Pistol",b,100,B.dq,B.uK,0,o,0,B.aQ,o,!1),A.bf(B.N1,"Explosive Heavy Pistol",b,100,B.d6,B.uK,0,o,0,B.aQ,o,!1),A.bf(B.N2,"Explosive Very Heavy Pistol",b,100,B.dJ,B.uK,0,o,0,B.aQ,o,!1),A.bf(B.N3,"Explosive Slug",b,100,B.fB,B.uK,0,o,0,B.aQ,o,!1),A.bf(B.N4,"Explosive Rifle",b,100,B.cg,B.uK,0,o,0,B.aQ,o,!1),A.bf(B.N5,"Explosive Arrow",b,100,B.dQ,B.uK,0,o,0,B.aQ,o,!1),A.bf(B.N6,"High Precision Medium Pistol",a,100,B.dq,B.uJ,0,o,0,B.aQ,o,!1),A.bf(B.N7,"High Precision Heavy Pistol",a,100,B.d6,B.uJ,0,o,0,B.aQ,o,!1),A.bf(B.N8,"High Precision Very Heavy Pistol",a,100,B.dJ,B.uJ,0,o,0,B.aQ,o,!1),A.bf(B.N9,"High Precision Slug",a,100,B.fB,B.uJ,0,o,0,B.aQ,o,!1),A.bf(B.Na,"High Precision Rifle",a,100,B.cg,B.uJ,0,o,0,B.aQ,o,!1),A.bf(B.Nb,"High Precision Arrow",a,100,B.dQ,B.uJ,0,o,0,B.aQ,o,!1),A.bf(B.Nc,"High Velocity Medium Pistol",a0,40,B.dq,B.De,0,o,0,B.aQ,o,!1),A.bf(B.Nd,"High Velocity Heavy Pistol",a0,40,B.d6,B.De,0,o,0,B.aQ,o,!1),A.bf(B.Ne,"High Velocity Very Heavy Pistol",a0,40,B.dJ,B.De,0,o,0,B.aQ,o,!1),A.bf(B.Nf,"High Velocity Rifle",a0,40,B.cg,B.De,0,o,0,B.aQ,o,!1),A.bf(B.Ng,"Hyper Expansive Medium Pistol",a1,100,B.dq,B.rT,0,o,0,B.aQ,o,!1),A.bf(B.Nh,"Hyper Expansive Heavy Pistol",a1,100,B.d6,B.rT,0,o,0,B.aQ,o,!1),A.bf(B.Ni,"Hyper Expansive Very Heavy Pistol",a1,100,B.dJ,B.rT,0,o,0,B.aQ,o,!1),A.bf(B.Nj,"Hyper Expansive Slug",a1,100,B.fB,B.rT,0,o,0,B.aQ,o,!1),A.bf(B.Nk,"Hyper Expansive Rifle",a1,100,B.cg,B.rT,0,o,0,B.aQ,o,!1),A.bf(B.Nl,"Hyper Expansive Shotgun Shell",a1,100,B.ea,B.rT,0,o,0,B.aQ,o,!1),A.bf(B.Nm,"Hyper Expansive Arrow",a1,100,B.dQ,B.rT,0,o,0,B.aQ,o,!1),A.bf(B.Nn,"Serrated Arrow",a2,30,B.dQ,B.aIh,0,o,0,B.aQ,o,!1),A.bf(B.No,"Hollow Point Medium Pistol",a2,30,B.dq,B.xS,0,o,0,B.aQ,o,!1),A.bf(B.Np,"Hollow Point Heavy Pistol",a2,30,B.d6,B.xS,0,o,0,B.aQ,o,!1),A.bf(B.Nq,"Hollow Point Very Heavy Pistol",a2,30,B.dJ,B.xS,0,o,0,B.aQ,o,!1),A.bf(B.Nr,"Hollow Point Slug",a2,30,B.fB,B.xS,0,o,0,B.aQ,o,!1),A.bf(B.Ns,"Hollow Point Rifle",a2,30,B.cg,B.xS,0,o,0,B.aQ,o,!1),A.bf(B.Nt,"Tracer Medium Pistol",a3,40,B.dq,B.Dd,0,o,0,B.aQ,o,!1),A.bf(B.Nu,"Tracer Heavy Pistol",a3,40,B.d6,B.Dd,0,o,0,B.aQ,o,!1),A.bf(B.Nv,"Tracer Very Heavy Pistol",a3,40,B.dJ,B.Dd,0,o,0,B.aQ,o,!1),A.bf(B.Nw,"Tracer Rifle",a3,40,B.cg,B.Dd,0,o,0,B.aQ,o,!1),A.bf(B.Nx,"C9 Charge","Plastic explosive, handmade, and guaranteed to explode.\n\nThis is an Explosive. A C9 Charge can be planted as an Action on any surface. Upon planting C9, the user attempts a DV17 Demolitions Skill Check. If they succeed, the C9 deals 8d6 damage when it explodes like an Armor Piercing Grenade. If they fail, it will deal 5d6 damage instead. Once planted, the charge takes 30 seconds (10 Rounds) to become \u201carmed.\u201d\n\nWhen planted, the Charge must be set to either remotely detonate (within a mile, anytime after armed, doing so takes an Action) or on a countdown (anywhere from immediately once armed to one week). The DV to defuse a C9 Charge as an Action with a Demolitions Skill Check is equal to the Skill Check it was planted with. Failing a Check to disarm a Charge or attempting to move the Charge from where it was planted causes it to explode.",250,B.de,B.eT,0,8,0,B.aQ,o,!1),A.bf(B.Ny,"C9 Kill Switch","When preventing equipment from falling into enemy hands, C9 is the only way to be sure.A C9 Kill Switch can be installed as part of a C9 Charge being planted by a user with authorized access on a Vehicle with a Security Upgrade, an ACPA or External Linear Frame with an Authorization Handshake Port, a Weapon with a Smartgun Link, or Cyberdeck with a DNA Lock. Once planted, a Kill Switch will cause the charge to explode when an unauthorized user attempts to access the device. \n\nAssuming the C9 was properly set up with a DV17 Demolitions Skill Check, a Kill Switch is guaranteed to destroy the device in the blast beyond repair. The existence of a Kill Switch installed in a piece of tech is normally trivial to detect when examined up close, but can be hidden using the Conceal/Reveal Object Skill. A C9 Kill Switch can be disarmed by disarming the C9 Charge it is installed in.",100,B.de,B.eT,0,8,0,B.aQ,o,!1),A.bf(B.Nz,"Mini C9 Charge","A tightly packed plastic explosive charge, smaller, for jobs that require less explosive. \n\nThis is an Explosive. A Mini C9 Charge can be planted as an Action on any surface. Upon planting C9, the user attempts a DV17 Demolitions Skill Check. If they succeed, the C9 deals 6d6 damage when it explodes like an Armor Piercing Grenade. If they fail, it will deal 4d6 damage instead. Once planted, the charge takes 30 seconds (10 Rounds) to become \u201carmed.\u201d \n\nWhen planted, the Charge must be set to either remotely detonate (within a mile, anytime after armed, doing so takes an Action) or on a countdown (anywhere from immediately once armed to one week). The DV to defuse a Charge as an Action with a Demolitions Skill Check is equal to the Skill Check it was planted with. Failing a Check to disarm a Charge or attempting to move the Charge from where it was planted causes it to explode.",60,B.de,B.eT,0,6,0,B.aQ,o,!1),A.bf(B.NA,"Arrowhypo","A reinforced airhypo custom-fitted onto the end of a carefully counterbalanced arrow, for use by specialist archers. \n\nEach unit of this ammunition can be loaded with one dose of a Street Drug. When using this ammunition, you deal no damage with your attack. Instead, anyone meat hit by your attack is injected with a dose of whatever street drug it was loaded with (if any). This ammunition may be recovered after firing just like a Basic Arrow.",100,B.dQ,B.aId,0,o,0,B.aQ,o,!1)],A.a1("J<nf>"))
for(q=A.K([B.NB,B.de,B.NC,B.h4],t.Ga,t.Bg).gbw().gM(0);q.q();){p=q.gF()
a4.push(A.bf(p.a,"Airburst Grenade","Sixteen coin-sized sensors in each unit of this gas-dispersal munition maximize the effective area of the payload to maximize tactical advantage.\n\nEach unit of this ammunition must be loaded with three doses of a single Street Drug to function. When using this ammunition, you deal no damage with your attack. Instead, anyone meat hit by your attack is gassed with a dose of whatever Street Drug it was loaded with. These effects of the gas are prevented by nasal filters, gas masks, and similar equipment.",125,p.b,B.aIc,0,o,0,B.aQ,o,!1))}a4.push(A.bf(B.ND,"CO2 Grenade","C02 grenades are the future of firefighting in urban environments, especially where water is a dwindling resource. They also excel in rural areas where fire hydrants may be scarce or inoperable.\n\nThis is Grenade Ammunition. It can be loaded into a Grenade Launcher or thrown. A CO2 Grenade does no damage. Instead, it extinguishes all instances of fire within the explosion area (see CP:R page 174). Any weapon capable of firing Smoke Grenades can also fire CO2 Grenades.",50,B.de,B.a44,0,o,0,B.dE,o,!1))
a4.push(A.bf(B.NE,"Hello Cutie Chromatic Rave Grenade","Play it loud, play it bright, play it anywhere! Chromatic Rave Grenades turn any situation into a party. Just throw one to transform a drab location into the hottest club around. A chip slot in each grenade ensures it will play the tunes you pick out! When the party\u2019s over? The grenade explodes into a shower of glitter and chromatic smoke to end things with a festive bang!\n\nThis is Grenade Ammunition. It cannot be loaded into a Grenade Launcher. When thrown, the grenade sticks to a surface in the square it landed in and initiates a thumping bass beat and colorful light show (either in generic techno club style or using the music from an inserted Memory Chip). Anyone who starts their Turn within a 10 m/yd by 10 m/yd (5 Square by 5 Square) area centered on the grenade during the show must succeed at a DV13 Concentration Check or suffer a -2 penalty to all Checks until the end of their Turn. The light and sound show lasts for 2 Rounds. At the top of the third Round, the grenade explodes, acting like a Smoke Grenade (see CP:R page 347) but with much more glitter. If a Memory Chip was slotted into the grenade, it is destroyed by the explosion.",50,B.de,B.rS,0,o,0,B.i8,o,!1))
a4.push(A.bf(B.CU,"Janus Hex Heavy Scent Balls","Janus Hex Heavy Scent Balls come in packs of 4, costing 20eb (Costly) each. Every Scent Ball is marked with the face of one of the idol groups four members. This proprietary ammunition cannot be modified or fabricated by a Tech unless they possess Maker Rank 6 or higher.",20,B.nV,B.rS,0,o,0,B.i8,o,!1))
a4.push(A.bf(B.CV,"Dazzle Dazzle ModBall","Acts as Flashbang Ammunition (see CP:R page 346) but only for a single target hit by a successful attack. This will also ignite a target hit by a Splashie ModBall. ",10,B.nV,B.rS,0,o,0,B.i8,o,!1))
a4.push(A.bf(B.CW,"Mega Ouchie ModBall","Acts as Biotoxin Ammunition (see CP:R page 345). ",20,B.nV,B.rS,0,o,0,B.i8,o,!1))
a4.push(A.bf(B.CX,"Ouchie ModBall","Acts as Poison Ammunition (see CP:R page 346). ",10,B.nV,B.rS,0,o,0,B.i8,o,!1))
a4.push(A.bf(B.CY,"Slippy ModBall","Balls filled with a slippery lubricant. If a Slippy ModBall is fired at a target they take no damage but gain a +1 Bonus to Contortionist Checks and to Brawling Checks to avoid or escape a grapple. If a Slippy ModBall is instead fired at a patch of ground, a 2 m/yd x 2 m/yd (1 Square) area is covered with the lubricant. Anyone attempting to stand on or pass through the area must succeed at a DV13 Athletics Check or fall Prone (see CP:R page 169) to the ground. Multiple instances of these effects cannot be stacked. Removing the lubricant requires 5 minutes of washing with water. The lubricant dries after 1 hour. Once dry, it is no longer slippery or effective. ",5,B.nV,B.rS,0,o,0,B.i8,o,!1))
a4.push(A.bf(B.CZ,"Splashie ModBalls","Balls of paint available in a variety of colors. This ammunition does no damage, but the paint is highly flammable. If a target splattered with the paint is exposed to an ignition source, they are set on fire. Until an Action is spent to put the target out, they take 2 damage directly to their HP whenever they end their Turn. Multiple instances of this cannot be stacked. Removing the paint requires 5 minutes of washing with water. ",5,B.nV,B.rS,0,o,0,B.i8,o,!1))
B.e.fR(a4)
return a4})
s($,"do1","cVQ",()=>A.VX())
s($,"do0","aie",()=>{var q,p,o,n,m,l,k,j,i,h="Favored by Nomads and other \u2018punks who ride bikes.",g=null,f="Can be made into clothes, vests, jackets, business suits, and even bikinis.",e="A combination of Kevlar\xae and plastic meshes inserted into the weave of the fabric.",d="Skinsuit with impact absorbing, sintered armorgel layered in key body areas. Also has a place to store your Cyberdeck and supports your Interface Plugs.",c="Heavier Armorjack, with solid plastic plating, reinforced with thicker Kevlar\xae mesh.",b="The thickest Armorjack, combining denser Kevlar\xae and a layered mix of plastic and mesh weaves.",a="Metalgear\xae will stop almost anything, but you're going to be easier to hit than a one-legged bantha in a potho race.",a0=5000,a1="black_chrome/torrel_chiang_fashion.jpg",a2="black_chrome/zhukova_fashion.jpg",a3=1000,a4="black_chrome/gibson_fashion.jpg",a5="black_chrome/montage_fashion.jpg",a6="black_chrome/zonda_fashion.jpg",a7="TUp Kevlar",a8="TUp Light Armorjack",a9="TUp Medium Armorjack",b0="TUp Heavy Armorjack",b1="TUp Subdermal Armor",b2="User's body and head armored at SP12. Does not stack with worn Armor. Ablates. Recovers 1 SP per day of rest.",b3="Scavenged Armor",b4="\u201cJudie makes these. She does good work and even incorporates clasps and other comfort features. Good armor can be expensive. This solves the problem with a little hard work and scrappy ingenuity. Way to go, Judie!\u201d\n\nScavenged Armor is head or body armor (each bought separately) with SP11. Once ablated, its SP cannot be restored. At 0 SP, it falls off the wearer.",b5="The heat of some battlefields rival the fires of hell. Our maximum hardplate model provides maximum clamshell protection to survive the most intense firefights.\n\nHeavy Metalgear\xae is Metalgear\xae with an SP of 19 and an Armor Penalty of -4 to REF, -5 to DEX, and -5 to MOVE.",b6="The needs of the battlefield are unceasing, and demand the perfect blend of offense and defense. Our half-segmented model provides the same all-over clamshell protection you expect from Metalgear\xae with the knee and elbow mobility you love about Light Metalgear\xae.\n\nHybrid Metalgear\xae is Metalgear\xae with an SP of 17 and an Armor Penalty of -3 to REF, -4 to DEX, and -4 to MOVE.",b7="The ultimate in full combat protection has just evolved. Today\u2019s battlefields are faster than those of yesterday. Our lighter model provides the same all-over clamshell protection you expect from us in a more mobile package than ever before. Segmentation is the new modularity.\n\nLight Metalgear\xae is Metalgear\xae with an SP of 16 and an Armor Penalty of -3 to REF, DEX, and MOVE.",b8="Magnetically seated armor panels are installed onto hardpoints drilled directly into the body. The panels are hot-swappable to keep the fight going until the enemy has been neutralized.\n\nBorgware. External Body Cyberware. Installation requires BODY 16 or higher unless the user is a Full Body Conversion. After installation, the user\u2019s body and head are armored at SP 15, and the user takes an Armor Penalty of -2 to REF, DEX, and MOVE. As an Action, the user can jettison their Dragoon Plating, removing the provided SP and freeing them of the Armor Penalty. \n\nIf the user is not equipped with a set of Dragoon Plating, they can activate the magnetic call system as an Action and summon a set of unattached plating within 6m/yds to them. The selected plating then flies through the air and attaches itself to the user. \n\nDragoon Plating contains nanomachines that repair it for 1 point of lost SP at the end of each day in which it does not lose SP. Additional sets of Dragoon Plating can be purchased for 1,000eb (Very Expensive). Ordering custom designs and colors adds 100eb to the cost.",b9="Custom-engineered magnetically seated Metalgear armor panels are installed onto specially designed heavy hardpoints drilled directly into the body. The panels are hot-swappable to keep the fight going until the enemy is reduced to ash.\n\nBorgware. External Body Cyberware. Installation requires BODY 16 or higher unless the user is a Full Body Conversion. After installation, the user\u2019s body and head are armored at SP 18, and the user takes an Armor Penalty of -3 to REF, DEX, and MOVE. As an Action, the user can jettison their Metalgear Dragoon Plating, removing the provided SP and freeing them of the Armor Penalty. \n\nIf the user is currently not equipped with a set of Metalgear Dragoon Plating, they can activate the magnetic call system as an Action and summon a set of unattached plating within 6m/yds to them. The selected plating then flies through the air and attaches itself to the user. \n\nMetalgear Dragoon Plating contains nanomachines that repair it for 1 point of lost SP at the end of each day in which it does not lose SP. Additional sets of Metalgear Dragoon Plating can be purchased for 5,000eb (Luxury). Ordering custom designs and colors adds 100eb to the cost.",c0="Standard Subdermal Armor isn\u2019t cutting it anymore, and Skinweave never did for you to begin with! You need hard plates under your skin to keep up with the firepower people are packing these days. Big, heavy ones that stop a bullet cold.\n\nBorgware. External Body Cyberware. Subdermal Armor. Installation requires BODY 10 unless the user is a Full Body Conversion. The user\u2019s body and head are armored at SP 13. The user takes an Armor Penalty of -2 to REF, DEX, and MOVE unless they have a BODY 14 or higher or are a Full Body Conversion, in which case the penalty is negated. Whenever the user successfully completes a full day of natural healing, nanomachines present in the plating repair both the body and the head location for one point of lost SP.\n\nNote: When installed in a Full Body Conversion, Subdermal Armor isn\u2019t usually subdermal but acts as the user\u2019s skin, complete with sensory (touch) capabilities.",c1=A.d8(B.bc,B.dS,"Leather Armor",h,4,20,0,g,B.x,!1,g,g,g),c2=A.d8(B.cu,B.f5,"Leather Helmet",h,4,20,0,g,B.x,!1,g,g,g),c3=A.d8(B.b1,B.dS,"Kevlar Armor",f,7,50,0,g,B.x,!1,g,g,g),c4=A.d8(B.bt,B.f5,"Kevlar Helmet",f,7,50,0,g,B.x,!1,g,g,g),c5=A.d8(B.aM,B.dS,"Light Armorjack Armor",e,11,100,0,g,B.x,!1,g,g,g),c6=A.d8(B.aW,B.f5,"Light Armorjack Helmet",e,11,100,0,g,B.x,!1,g,g,g),c7=A.d8(B.p6,B.dS,"Bodyweight Suit",d,11,500,0,g,B.x,!1,g,g,g),c8=A.d8(B.qi,B.f5,"Bodyweight Helmet",d,11,500,0,g,B.x,!1,g,g,g),c9=A.d8(B.fL,B.dS,"Medium Armorjack Armor",c,12,100,2,g,B.x,!1,g,g,g),d0=A.d8(B.fM,B.f5,"Medium Armorjack Helmet",c,12,100,2,g,B.x,!1,g,g,g),d1=A.d8(B.ki,B.dS,"Heavy Armorjack Armor",b,13,500,2,g,B.x,!1,g,g,g),d2=A.d8(B.l1,B.f5,"Heavy Armorjack Helmet",b,13,500,2,g,B.x,!1,g,g,g),d3=A.d8(B.xU,B.dS,"Flak Armor","This is the 21st century version of the time honored flak vest and pants.",15,500,4,g,B.x,!1,g,g,g),d4=A.d8(B.xV,B.f5,"Flak Helmet","This is the 21st century version of the time honored flak helmet.",15,500,4,g,B.x,!1,g,g,g),d5=A.d8(B.Di,B.dS,"Metalgear\xae Armor",a,18,a0,4,g,B.x,!1,g,g,g),d6=A.d8(B.Dj,B.f5,"Metalgear\xae Helmet",a,18,a0,4,g,B.x,!1,g,g,g),d7=A.d8(B.eU,B.lM,"Bulletproof Shield","A transparent polycarbonate shield that can protect you in a firefight.",10,100,0,g,B.x,!1,g,g,g),d8=A.d8(B.OF,B.dS,"Corporate Island","Looking for that island style but need that corporate appearance? Nu-Tek has just the outfit for you!\n\nCrafted from static-free, tear-proof synthetic silk, the Corporate Island line slides right over cyberware and concealed weapons. So, while the other guy is looking like a stiff, you can flex all you want and not worry about having to replace your beautiful outfit!\n\nThe Corporate Island comes in two styles: dress and casual. The dress style is totally corporate, with solid colors, and is wrinkle-free. The casual style includes pastels and island prints and is not wrinkle-free.\n\nThe Corporate Island is Light Armorjack Body Armor with the appearance of Businesswear Fashion.",11,500,0,g,B.ak,!1,g,a1,g),d9=A.d8(B.OG,B.dS,"The Dirk Combat Jacket","Nothing says style like the Dirk Combat Jacket. This fine synthetic leather jacket, reinforced with a thick layer of Kevlar\xae, is popular with Solos who like to party. The Dirk isn\u2019t a long coat, but instead a puffy coat that offers not only protection but space to store guns and clips.\n\nThey say when a Solo hits the dance floor in a Dirk, it means they are out for blood, and someone is going to die. The Dirk\u2019s design allows for quick movement, crashing through windows and breaking through the occasional table. The Dirk is manufactured by Zhukova International, a Russian fashion company specializing in trendy wear for \u201cruffians.\u201d\n\nThe Dirk is Light Armorjack Body Armor with the appearance of Leisurewear Fashion. \n\nTwo standard-size clips of ammunition can be concealed in the jacket without a Check.",11,500,0,g,B.ak,!1,g,a2,g),e0=A.d8(B.OH,B.dS,"Executive Armor","When it comes to prestige and class, the name Torrell and Chiang stands above the rest. Night City\u2019s premiere apparelists now offer custom-tailored executive armor. Each suit is made from Kevlar\xae layered with ceramic plating and is completely stain-resistant.\n\nGot dirt or oil on your suit? Hose it down and it\u2019s as good as new. Got an embarrassing bullet hole? Just wait, and let the suit\u2019s nanomachines fix it for you. Don\u2019t settle for peasantwear when you can dress like a noble of old. Torrell and Chiang: keeping prestige modern.\n\nTorrell and Chiang Executive Armor is Light Armorjack Body Armor with the appearance of Businesswear Fashion. \n\nEach day that the Torrell and Chiang Executive Armor does not lose SP, nanomachines present in the armor repair it for 1 point of lost SP. ",11,a3,0,g,B.ak,!1,g,a1,g),e1=A.d8(B.OI,B.dS,"Fire Brand Bunker Gear","When it comes to reliable gear for firefighters, nothing says fireproof like Fire Brand. Based out of Texas, Fire Brand emerged in 2040 with gear guaranteed to be both fireproof and bulletproof. Crafted from state-of-the-art materials, Bunker Gear consists of a jacket with a hood that slides under the helmet, leggings that seal tight around the ankles of the boots, and sleeves that do the same around the gloves. Plus both a built-in gas mask and oxygen tank! The next time you need to head into the Combat Zone to fight a four-alarm fire, go in prepared. Go in Fire Brand!\n\nFire Brand Bunker Gear is Flak Armor. Unlike other armor, it isn\u2019t bought in two pieces and must always be worn on both your body and head locations. When repaired, both pieces are repaired at the same time. When the armor is worn, the user is immune to being damaged by fire (including incendiary ammunition) and cannot be set on fire. \n\nThe helmet comes with a built-in gas mask they can choose to slide down and activate without an Action. If the gas mask is activated the user is immune to the effects of toxic gasses, fumes, and all similar dangers that must be inhaled. In addition, the armor comes with an oxygen tank hooked up to the gas mask, which contains 30 minutes of air, before the tank must be refilled from the ambient atmosphere, which takes 1 hour.",14,a3,4,g,B.ak,!1,g,a2,g),e2=A.d8(B.Dk,B.dS,"Laser Light Street Jacket","Whether slamming at a club or prowling dark alleys, the Laser Light Street Jacket is a must-have for the modern dance floor hustler. These fine black synthetic leather jackets, lined with Kevlar\xae and weave, stand out in a crowd thanks to their fiber optic lighting displays. Each jacket comes with an internal rechargeable battery.\n\nThe fiber optics can produce the following light displays: solid black light, strobe black light, solid red, strobe red, solid green, strobe green, solid white, strobe white, club scene streaming, club scene strobe, firefight ignite (flashes red every time the trigger is pulled if you have a gun connected to a Smartgun Link) and off.\n\nDon\u2019t be caught on the streets without one!\n\nA Laser Light Jacket is Light Armorjack Body Armor with the appearance of Urban Flash Fashion. Additionally, it counts as 1 installation of Light Tattoo Fashionware when worn, making it helpful for reaching the +2 Wardrobe and Style bonus for having 3 installations of Light Tattoo.",11,500,0,g,B.ak,!1,g,a4,g),e3=A.d8(B.OJ,B.xT,"Lotos Netsuit","When it comes to fashion and netrunning, nothing says efficiency, flash, and sleek like the Lotos Netsuit by indie designer Lotos. This netsuit allows the user to link to and manage their Cyberdeck with ease. The suit is lined with ceramic and titanium plating, with an underlying nanotube layer. This makes the Lotos a must-have for Netrunners on the go who find themselves caught up in firefights. Lotos makes these suits custom for her clientele; they don\u2019t come cheap but are worth every cent.\n\nWearing a Lotos Netsuit gives your Cyberdeck 1 extra slot (stored on the suit instead of the Cyberdeck) that can only be used for Hardware. When you take off the Netsuit, Hardware on the suit is automatically uninstalled from the Cyberdeck. Unlike other armor, a Lotos Netsuit isn\u2019t bought in two pieces, and must always be worn on both your body and head location. Each location has its own SP13, and while worn, lowers the user\u2019s REF, DEX and MOVE by 2. When repaired, both pieces are repaired at the same time. You can\u2019t wear a Netsuit with similar armor or fashion, such as a Bodyweight Suit. Every purchase comes with an Excellent Quality Cyberdeck (see CP:R page 351).",13,a0,2,g,B.ak,!1,g,a4,g),e4=A.d8(B.OK,B.dS,"Masetto AirRider","The Masetto AirRider is a motorcycle suit with a built-in airbag system. Constructed out of a rubberized Kevlar\xae blend, the AirRider inflates in the event of a crash using a CO2 cartridge that slots comfortably next to a back-fitted water bottle. So next time you hit the highway for some two-wheeled action, be smart and be prepared to bounce with AirRider!\n\nThe AirRider is Kevlar\xae Body Armor. Whenever the user would experience the Whiplash Critical Injury as a result of a crash, the AirRider inflates to prevent it. Once inflated, the user\u2019s MOVE is reduced by 5 (minimum 1) until the AirRider is deflated with an Action. After being inflated once, the AirRider\u2019s 20eb (Everyday) CO2 tank must be replaced until it can be used again (otherwise the rider will look like a saggy baggy elephant).",7,100,0,g,B.ak,!1,g,a5,g),e5=A.d8(B.OL,B.f5,"MechaMan Motorcycle Helmet","Looking for that machine look while flying down the highway on your turbo-charged street bike? Want to catch the attention of your next potential input/output? Then grab the Tokyo Dynamics MechaMan motorcycle helmet! This stylish, futuristic helmet is fully illuminated for riding without headlights past sunset. It even runs a built-in HUD display to really drive home that robot feel. The helmet has built-in speakers for both interior and exterior use and can link to your Agent. Each MechaMan is manufactured from a ceramic and metal framework, making it super durable. Putting on the MechaMan is ultra-easy, with a clam feature that closes after the user\u2019s head is in place.\n\nThe MechaMan Motorcycle Helmet is Flak Head Armor with built-in Tech upgraded Smart Glasses, which come installed with Chyron and Low Light / Infrared / UV Cybereye options.",15,a0,4,g,B.ak,!1,g,a6,g),e6=A.d8(B.OM,B.dS,"Mimic Clothing Kit","Designed for the individual who wants to keep their personal style without sacrificing protection. Included in every box is a complete set of molded ceramic plates and ballistic fiber segments designed to attach to your favorite clothing and suitable for any body type. Turn your favorite sweater into your favorite armored sweater with no pesky sewing required!\n\nA Mimic Clothing Kit can be combined with any Fashion Jacket or Top to turn it into a piece of Light Armorjack Body Armor with the appearance of the appropriate Fashion. Once combined, removing the armor plates is impossible. Each kit can make one piece of Body Armor.",11,100,0,g,B.ak,!1,g,a5,g),e7=A.d8(B.ON,B.dS,"Montage Variable Clothing Line","With Montage\u2019s new Variable Clothing Line, color coordination is a hassle of the past! These smart clothing pieces change color and pattern to match the user\u2019s desires. Each piece is crafted from programmable micro-imaging fibers and connected to a chip that stores style information. Using your Agent, link to the chip and upload your style for the day. Be camouflage one day and go khaki casual the next with no fuss! Each variable comes with three standard programmed styles. To buy more, visit Montage on the Data Pool! With Montage, there\u2019s less fuss and more fashion!\n\nThe Montage Variable Clothing Line is Light Armorjack with the appearance of either Generic Chic or Gang Colors, depending on which color/pattern is being displayed. With an Action, a user can change between purchased colors/patterns using a paired Agent. The chip comes preprogrammed with three colors/patterns of the buyer\u2019s choice. Additional colors/patterns cost 20eb (Everyday) each and can be purchased and downloaded from an Agent in as little as 1 minute.",11,500,0,g,B.ak,!1,g,a5,g),e8=A.d8(B.OO,B.dS,"Shock Armor","Gibson Battlegear specifically designed their Shock Armor for prison use. A corrections officer wearing the Shock Armor not only has the benefit of a Kevlar\xae suit but the uniform is also lined with microfilament capacitors capable of delivering a powerful shock to anyone touching it.\n\nThe interior of the armor is rubber-lined, offering immunity to the outer charge. Shock Armor is widely issued in private prisons in the United States as the armor has proven capable of reducing the abundance of prison riots by a significant margin.\n\nGibson Battlegear Shock Armor is Kevlar\xae Body Armor. When you are the defender in a grapple, you can use an Action to send a pulse of electricity into the armor, forcing the attacker in the grapple to make a DV15 Resist Torture/Drugs Check. If they fail, the grapple ends immediately.",7,500,0,g,B.ak,!1,g,a2,g),e9=A.d8(B.OP,B.dS,"SkidRow Trench","The SkidRow Trench by SkidRow Limited is a stylish take on the classic trench coat. Coming in a variety of colors, from film noir gray to flamboyant pink, this armored fashion statement tells the world you\u2019ve got both style and substance.\n\nLined with durable armor plating, this jacket has proven popular with Execs who like a little mystery in their wardrobe. Even Fixers have been drawn to the deep pockets provided by the trench coat. \n\nThe price isn\u2019t bad either, which helps keep SkidRow Limited relevant in the fashion industry. It is pretty heavy, though.\n\nThe SkidRow Trench is Flak Body Armor with an SP of 13 instead of 15.",13,100,4,g,B.ak,!1,g,a5,g),f0=A.d8(B.OQ,B.dS,"Street Viper Riding Suit","When it comes to the best in riding suits, the Street Viper comes out on top. Produced by Zonda, the Street Viper Riding Suit is manufactured from Kevlar\xae with a special low-friction layer incorporated into elbow blades, designed to aid in sliding. The blades are responsible for Viper\u2019s unique silhouette and are quite sharp. Zonda offers their riding suit in dozens of assorted designs, the most popular schemes being black with red blades, and neon yellow with black blades. More than just being an excellent suit, this feature has boosted the popularity of the Street Viper, making it a perfect fashion choice for any occasion, whether you arrived on a bike or not. Friday night at the Afterlife, you are bound to see someone wearing a Street Viper.\n\nThe Street Viper Riding Suit is Kevlar\xae Body Armor that incorporates 2 Medium Melee Weapons into the design. The weapons are always considered drawn while the armor is being worn.",7,100,0,g,B.ak,!1,g,a6,g),f1=A.d8(B.OR,B.xT,"Tactical Smart Armor","Gibson Battlegear Tactical Smart Armor is a popular combat armor worn by many Solos in the post-4th Corporate War United States. Reminiscent of old-school SWAT gear, Tactical Smart Armor offers innovative technology and high durability. The armor includes elbow, knee, and shin guards crafted from Kevlar\xae and ballistic-proof plastics.\n\nAdditionally, the integrated helmet is constructed from high-density polymers and comes with built-in Smart Glasses. With all of this armor, a Solo can confidently storm into a safehouse and withstand at least the first volley of gunfire almost completely unharmed.\n\nThe Gibson Battlegear Tactical Smart Armor is Medium Armorjack Armor with built-in Smart Glasses. Unlike other armor, it isn\u2019t bought in two pieces and must always be worn on both your body and head location. When repaired, both pieces are repaired at the same time.",12,a3,2,g,B.ak,!1,g,a4,g),f2=A.d8(B.OS,B.f5,a7,"",8,500,0,g,B.az,!0,g,g,g),f3=A.d8(B.Dl,B.dS,a7,"",8,500,0,g,B.az,!0,g,g,g),f4=A.d8(B.p5,B.f5,a8,"",12,a3,0,g,B.az,!0,g,g,g),f5=A.d8(B.nY,B.dS,a8,"",12,a3,0,g,B.az,!0,g,g,g),f6=A.d8(B.qg,B.f5,a9,"",12,a3,1,g,B.az,!0,g,g,g),f7=A.d8(B.qh,B.dS,a9,"",12,a3,1,g,B.az,!0,g,g,g),f8=A.d8(B.xW,B.f5,b0,"",14,a0,0,g,B.az,!0,g,g,g),f9=A.d8(B.uN,B.dS,b0,"",14,a0,0,g,B.az,!0,g,g,g),g0=A.d8(B.Dn,B.dS,"TUp Bodyweight Suit",d,12,100,0,g,B.az,!0,g,g,g),g1=A.d8(B.Dm,B.f5,"TUp Bodyweight Helmet",d,12,100,0,g,B.az,!0,g,g,g),g2=A.d8(B.uO,B.f5,b1,b2,12,a3,0,g,B.az,!0,g,g,g),g3=A.d8(B.uP,B.dS,b1,b2,12,a3,0,g,B.az,!0,g,g,g),g4=A.d8(B.lN,B.dS,b3,b4,11,50,0,g,B.fa,!1,g,g,g),g5=A.d8(B.xX,B.f5,b3,b4,11,50,0,g,B.fa,!1,g,g,g),g6=A.d8(B.nZ,B.dS,"Custom Armor","",0,0,0,g,B.x,!0,g,g,g),g7=t.Y,g8=t.S,g9=A.K([B.D,12],g7,g8)
g9=A.d8(B.OT,B.fK,"Arasaka Neo Guardian","Arasaka\u2019s Neo Guardian is used as a big scary bodyguard to protect valuable VIP clients. To remain at top-piloting efficiency around the clock, members of an Arasaka VIP Security Detail will rotate in and out of the same ACPA throughout the day. To minimize payroll expenses, Arasaka often seeks out FBCs for the grueling work.\n\nLinear Frame: Sigma\n\nShell: Light Metalgear\xae \n\nOnboard Weapons: Arasaka Takanami SMG (x2), Malorian Arms Sub-Flechette Gun, Stun Baton\n\nOnboard Cyberware: Internal Agent, Targeting Scope",16,17900,0,A.pr(B.fu,B.cP,A.K([B.a3,-1],g7,g8),B.cP,g9),B.aQ,!1,25,"solo_of_fortune/Araska Neo Guardian Blueprint.png",new A.aTb())
q=A.K([B.D,14],g7,g8)
q=A.d8(B.OU,B.fK,"Arasaka Neo Standard","Arasaka\u2019s standard line ACPA had to be reinvented after the 4th Corporate War, but the Neo Standard still bears many of the same hallmarks as its predecessor. It is designed with civilian targets in mind and has enough armor to defeat sustained small arms fire. Its use against protesters and would-be resistance groups has been well documented.\n\nLinear Frame: Beta\n\nShell: Light Metalgear\xae \n\nOnboard Weapons: Malorian Arms Sub-Flechette Gun, Tsunami Arms Type-18-S\n\nOnboard Cyberware: Internal Agent, Targeting Scope",16,25100,0,A.pr(B.fu,B.cP,A.K([B.C,1,B.y,-1,B.a3,-1],g7,g8),B.cP,q),B.aQ,!1,37,"solo_of_fortune/Araska Neo Standard Blueprint.png",new A.aTc())
p=A.K([B.D,16],g7,g8)
p=A.d8(B.OV,B.fK,"Arasaka Shin Daioni","The newest edition of Arasaka\u2019s  bogeyman ACPA remains entirely reliant on a highly skilled pilot for optimal battlefield efficiency. Pilots, typically highly modified FBCs, capable of bringing a DaiOni\u2019s full potential out are worth investment and protection, which Arasaka\u2019s cradle-to-grave employment excels in.\n\nLinear Frame: Omega\n\nShell: Heavy Metalgear\xae \n\nOnboard Weapons: Arasaka Neo Rapid Assault 16  (TUp +1 Attachment Slot) w/ Smartgun Link, Kendachi Mono-Three (x2), Midnight Arms Dawnmaker AMR w/ Sniper Scout Barrel, Tsunami Arms Type-18-S, Tsunami Arms Helix (Citrus Edition) w/ Smartgun Link\n\nOnboard Cyberware: Jump Booster, Targeting Scope, Teleoptics",19,61350,0,A.pr(B.fu,B.cP,A.K([B.C,-1],g7,g8),B.cP,p),B.aQ,!1,39,"solo_of_fortune/Arasaka Dai Oni.png",new A.aTd())
o=A.K([B.D,10],g7,g8)
o=A.d8(B.OW,B.fK,"Blueraven \u201cSewer Rat\u201d","A homegrown ACPA concept built by Night City weapons savant BlueRaven, the Sewer Rat is an ACPA designed \u201cto fit in tight spaces and in tight budgets,\u201d to \u201cprove the viability of locally sourced parts and solutions.\u201d. While it isn\u2019t the cheapest ACPA, it can theoretically be built with limited access to corporate resources, a fact which scares the powerful, just like Punknaughts do.\n\nLinear Frame: Salvaged\n\nShell: Salvaged\n\nOnboard Weapons: Scatter Ratter (x2)\n\nOnboard Cyberware: Popup Shield (x2)",14,14104,0,A.pr(B.fu,B.cP,A.K([B.C,-2,B.y,-1,B.a3,-1],g7,g8),B.cP,o),B.aQ,!1,23,"solo_of_fortune/Blueraven Sewer Rat.png",new A.aTe())
n=A.K([B.D,16],g7,g8)
n=A.d8(B.OX,B.fK,"Metacorp Nyx","MetaCorp\u2019s strategic capture of a former Mexican Metals factory allowed them to construct a modern version of the long out of print Nemesis Assault. By hollowing the Nemesis\u2019s armor out, MetaCorp engineers made room for sweeping upgrades to the system\u2019s Linear Frame. The result is an ACPA with a huge surplus of power, which translates directly into amazing speed, the perfect tool to defend the floating cities of New Galveston and the MetaKey from pirates.\n\nLinear Frame: Omega\n\nShell: Light Metalgear\xae \n\nOnboard Weapons: EQ Sniper Rifle w/ Drum Magazine & Sniper Rifle Rechamber, MetaCorp Chaingun \u201cVictoria\u201d\n\nOnboard Cyberware: Low Light/Infrared/UV, Radio Communicator, Web Foot",16,35400,0,A.pr(B.fu,B.cP,A.K([B.C,3,B.a3,-1],g7,g8),B.cP,n),B.aQ,!1,28,"solo_of_fortune/Meta Nyx.png",new A.aTf())
m=A.d8(B.OY,B.fK,"Militech Commando","As the battlefield workhorse of ACPAs, the Commando meshes seamlessly into Militech\u2019s standard operating squad tactics. On the front lines, it is fielded in small strike teams supported by artillery to hit already scouted positions. Depending on the battlefield conditions. Commando squads carry external weapons to supplement their onboard arsenal, favoring single-use rocket launchers especially when attacking fortified positions.\n\nLinear Frame: Beta\n\nShell: Hybrid Metalgear\xae \n\nOnboard Weapons: Militech MK.27 LMG, Militech Mountain Goat Rifle\n\nOnboard Cyberware: Low Light/Infrared/UV, Radio Communicator, Scrambler/Descrambler",17,25274,0,A.pr(B.fu,B.cP,B.fv,B.cP,A.K([B.D,14],g7,g8)),B.aQ,!1,30,"solo_of_fortune/Militech Commando.png",new A.aTg())
l=A.K([B.D,14],g7,g8)
l=A.d8(B.OZ,B.fK,"Sovoil Bombardier","A heavy ACPA built for an artillery support role, the SovOil Bombardier began its life as a Russian Arms design, before being purchased by its most prolific user, SovOil, in the modern era. In this manner, it and the Zhirafa Boris can be considered brothers. After extensive retooling to cut down on production costs, the modern Bombardier packs a comparable amount of battlefield destruction to the Boris into a 30% cheaper package.\n\nLinear Frame: Beta\n\nShell: Metalgear\xae \n\nOnboard Weapons: EQ Rocket Launcher w/ Drum Magazine & Long Tube (x4)\n\nOnboard Cyberware: None",18,32400,0,A.pr(B.fu,B.cP,A.K([B.C,-2,B.y,-1,B.a3,-1],g7,g8),B.cP,l),B.aQ,!1,51,"solo_of_fortune/SovOil Bombadier.png",new A.aTh())
k=A.K([B.D,12],g7,g8)
k=A.d8(B.P_,B.fK,"Tsunami Arms Magus","Originally designed as the ultimate information gathering command unit, the Tsunami Arms Magus soon found its niche as a designated sniper thanks to the glowing battlefield record of the \u201cDeathwind\u201d Railgun during the final days of the 4th Corporate War. This modern rendition, designed absent the involvement of original collaborator Raven MicroCybernetics, is an exercise in effectiveness, focusing the Magus on a sniper role to reduce the production cost significantly.\n\nLinear Frame: Sigma\n\nShell: Hybrid Metalgear\xae \n\nOnboard Weapons: Tsunami Arms \u201cDeathwind\u201d Railgun\n\nOnboard Cyberware: Grip Foot, Targeting Scope, TeleOptics",17,26624,0,A.pr(B.fu,B.cP,A.K([B.C,-1],g7,g8),B.cP,k),B.aQ,!1,25,"solo_of_fortune/Tsunami Arms Magus.png",new A.aTi())
j=A.K([B.D,12],g7,g8)
j=A.d8(B.P0,B.fK,"Zetatech Grasshopper","As the lightest ACPA on the market, the Zetatech Grasshopper has always existed as a midpoint between personnel-grade Metalgear\xae and its larger cousins. Yet, the first ever manufactured ACPA remains relevant even today! Modern urban conflict favors the Grasshopper\u2019s mobile and rugged usability. The Grasshopper has a special advantage over other ACPAs as well. It is the only ACPA on the market capable of fitting into the passenger seat of an unmodified vehicle. Squads of Grasshopper pilots riding motorcycles aren\u2019t an unusual site in urban conflict zones!\n\nLinear Frame: Sigma\n\nShell: Light Metalgear\xae \n\nOnboard Weapons: Militech \u201cBig Boomer\u201d\n\nOnboard Cyberware: Interface Plugs, Skate Foot",15,11600,0,A.pr(B.fu,B.cP,A.K([B.C,1],g7,g8),B.cP,j),B.aQ,!1,18,"solo_of_fortune/Zetatech Grasshopper.png",new A.aTj())
i=A.K([B.D,16],g7,g8)
return A.a([c1,c2,c3,c4,c5,c6,c7,c8,c9,d0,d1,d2,d3,d4,d5,d6,d7,d8,d9,e0,e1,e2,e3,e4,e5,e6,e7,e8,e9,f0,f1,f2,f3,f4,f5,f6,f7,f8,f9,g0,g1,g2,g3,g4,g5,g6,g9,q,p,o,n,m,l,k,j,A.d8(B.P1,B.fK,"Zhirafa Boris","The Zhirafa Boris is an update to the Boris of the 2020s, originally developed by Russian Arms. Zhirafa has seen fit to modify the core design of the Boris with added firepower and a new, heavier armor. In terms of modern conflicts, these huge ACPA see use mostly as a rally point for Neo-Soviet forces in tense border disputes. Recently, Boris have shown up in Tanzania on the side of the people of Tanzania, and on the politically-shattered northern half of the Korean peninsula, on the side of various warlords.\n\nLinear Frame: Omega\n\nShell: Heavy Metalgear\xae \n\nOnboard Weapons: EQ Rocket Launcher w/ Extended Magazine & Smartgun Link (x4), Techtronika Russia BMG-500 (Silver Edition)\n\nOnboard Cyberware: Targeting Scope",19,46900,0,A.pr(B.fu,B.cP,A.K([B.y,-1,B.a3,-1,B.C,-2],g7,g8),B.cP,i),B.aQ,!1,60,"solo_of_fortune/Zhirafa Boris.png",new A.aTk()),A.d8(B.P3,B.f5,"Heavy Metalgear\xae Helmet",b5,19,a0,0,A.pr(B.fu,B.cP,A.K([B.y,-4,B.a3,-5,B.C,-5],g7,g8),B.cP,B.fv),B.aQ,!1,g,g,g),A.d8(B.P2,B.dS,"Heavy Metalgear\xae Armor",b5,19,a0,0,A.pr(B.fu,B.cP,A.K([B.y,-4,B.a3,-5,B.C,-5],g7,g8),B.cP,B.fv),B.aQ,!1,g,g,g),A.d8(B.P5,B.f5,"Hybrid Metalgear\xae Helmet",b6,17,2552,0,A.pr(B.fu,B.cP,A.K([B.y,-3,B.a3,-4,B.C,-4],g7,g8),B.cP,B.fv),B.aQ,!1,g,g,g),A.d8(B.P4,B.dS,"Hybrid Metalgear\xae Armor",b6,17,2552,0,A.pr(B.fu,B.cP,A.K([B.y,-3,B.a3,-4,B.C,-4],g7,g8),B.cP,B.fv),B.aQ,!1,g,g,g),A.d8(B.P6,B.f5,"Light Metalgear\xae Helmet",b7,16,a3,3,g,B.aQ,!1,g,g,g),A.d8(B.Do,B.dS,"Light Metalgear\xae Armor",b7,16,a3,3,g,B.aQ,!1,g,g,g),A.d8(B.Dp,B.dS,"Dragoon Plating (Body)",b8,15,a0,2,g,B.dE,!0,g,g,g),A.d8(B.Dq,B.f5,"Dragoon Plating (Head)",b8,15,a0,2,g,B.dE,!0,g,g,g),A.d8(B.Dr,B.dS,"Dragoon Plating, Metalgear (Body)",b9,18,15e3,3,g,B.dE,!0,g,g,g),A.d8(B.Ds,B.f5,"Dragoon Plating, Metalgear (Head)",b9,18,15e3,3,g,B.dE,!0,g,g,g),A.d8(B.Dt,B.dS,"Heavy Subdermal Plating (Body)",c0,13,a0,2,g,B.dE,!0,g,g,g),A.d8(B.Du,B.f5,"Heavy Subdermal Plating (Head)",c0,13,a0,2,g,B.dE,!0,g,g,g),A.d8(B.P7,B.xT,"Esporma Environment Suit","The Esporma Environment Suit is a must for any situation that may include poisonous gasses, bioweapons, or radiation. All seams are magnetically sealed and air-tight. With an internal oxygen supply, the wearer can enter most hazardous situations without suffering ill-effects and the armor woven into the outer layer ensures it won\u2019t puncture easily. Best of all, the Esporma is self-repairing!\n\nUnlike other armor, the Esporma Environment Suit isn\u2019t bought in two pieces and must always be worn on both your body and head location. Each location has its own SP 8. When repaired, both pieces are repaired at the same time. Wearing an Esporma Environment Suit protects the user from radiation. The suit comes equipped with an oxygen tank which can provide up to 30 Minutes of air before the tank must be refilled from the ambient air, which takes 1 Hour. During each Hour that the Esporma Environment Suit does not lose SP, nanomachines repair it for 1 point of lost SP.",8,a0,0,g,B.m4,!1,g,g,g),A.d8(B.P8,B.lM,"Skidrow Packshield","Worried about your life and toting around your possessions? Worry no more! The PackShield from SkidRow Limited isn\u2019t just a stylish backpack loaded with ergonomically designed organizational pockets. Pull it off, press a button, and reinforced panels will unfold to transform this chic bag into a shield capable of stopping gunfi re. Classic fashion with a new twist!\n\nThe PackShield is a Bulletproof Shield (HP10) with the appearance of Businesswear. It will not provide protection while worn as a backpack and must still be equipped in a hand to be effective. When worn as a backpack it does not offer protection but does function as a carryall. The PackShield cannot be installed in Popup Shield cyberware.",10,100,0,g,B.m4,!1,g,g,g),A.d8(B.P9,B.lM,"High-Density Bulletproof Shield","When the cops realized their bosses were buying from the lowest bidder to provide crap shields to the department, they attempted a low-tech solution ... but the gangs quickly learned that acid would melt the duct tape holding multiple shields together. After nearly a hundred injuries resulting from \u201cshield malfunctions,\u201d the higher-ups got the message and commissioned this slightly better design.\n\nA shield with 15 HP. It cannot be installed in a Popup Shield.",15,200,0,g,B.jU,!1,g,g,g)],A.a1("J<yc>"))})
s($,"don","cGG",()=>A.VX())
s($,"dol","cW0",()=>A.K([B.lW,"Homeless, Ragged, Vagrant",B.l5,"Dangerous, Violent, Rebellious",B.l6,"Standard, Colorful, Modular",B.lX,"Folksy, Retro, Free-Spirited",B.lY,"Comfort, Agility, Athleticism",B.l7,"Western, Rugged, Tribal",B.km,"Bright, Costume-like, Youthful",B.l8,"Flashy, Technological, Streetwear",B.l9,"Leadership, Presence, Authority",B.la,"Exclusive, Designer, Couture",B.DE,"You\u2019re on the open road, being chased by a pack of GoGangers screaming for your blood. Slow down and they\u2019ll recycle both you and your bike for parts. So, you pull your pistol from its holster, look back at the pack\u2019s leader, extend your arm, and fire.\n\nLuckily, you\u2019re wearing a MechaMan Smart Glove from Tokyo Dynamics. It\u2019s not just a stylish biking glove perfect for keeping a firm hold on your bike during crap weather. It also comes with a built-in Subdermal Grip. That means the Smart Glove\u2019s always ready-set-go to enhance your aim and ensure your enemy hits the road the hard way.\n\nThe MechaMan Smart Glove comes preinstalled with a Subdermal Grip and has 1 additional Option Slot for a Cyberarm or Cyberlimb option. When worn, the options stored in the glove can be accessed. Putting on a Smart Glove and taking one off is an Action. The cost to purchase and install a Cyberarm or Cyberlimb option into the Smart Glove is the same cost as doing so in a Cyberarm. Any options stored in a Cyberhand or meat hand the Smart Glove is worn over are inaccessible while the Smart Glove is being worn. A Neural Link is still required to make use of the Subdermal Grip. Cannot be concealed. ",B.DD,"Forget ever doing laundry again! Going on a date and need an outfit, but don\u2019t have anything you like? Let Holo-Wear by Masetto Tech Clothing take care of that for you! Simply slap on the ankle, neck, waist, and wrist units, jump on your Agent, and download your outfit. Who needs closet space when you\u2019re wearing light sculpted by the best fashion designers in the industry!\n\nEach unit houses a compact holographic projector, working together with its mates to project the outfit over the customer\u2019s body. Instant style! Masetto does advise users to wear some form of underwear in case an EMP goes off.\n\nMasetto Holo-Wear gives the user the appearance of wearing clothing of the type shown by the hologram. With an Action, a user can change between purchased outfits using a paired Agent.\n\nEach Holo-Wear comes with one outfit for free, and additional outfits of any fashion can be purchased and downloaded from an Agent in as little as 1 minute at 100eb (Premium) each. If the user is hit by an EMP, Microwaver pulse, or similar effect their Masetto Holo-Wear automatically shuts down and remains inoperable for 1 minute. This is in addition to any other effects inflicted on their Cyberware or carried electronics. Bulky worn clothing or items may clip through the hologram",B.DF,""],A.a1("jy"),t.N))
s($,"dom","czH",()=>A.K([B.lW,"Стиль бродяжки",B.l5,"Цвета банды",B.l6,"Универсальный шик",B.lX,"Богемный",B.lY,"Одежда для отдыха",B.l7,"Кожа кочевников",B.km,"Азиатский поп",B.l8,"Городской шик",B.l9,"Деловая одежда",B.la,"Высокая мода",B.DE,"Mecha Man",B.DD,"Masetto Holo Wear",B.DF,"Custom Clothing"],A.a1("jy"),t.N))
